keel (0.23.62) unstable; urgency=medium

  * After a VIP claim, the new holder told its peers of the claim one
    after the other (keel#235). The dead old holder came first, so each
    other peer learnt the new route only after that peer's 10 s timeout.
    A mesh node outside the pair has no keel-vip-control and learns the
    route only from this message, so its clients sent to the dead node
    for about 10 s. The claim now goes to each peer in its own thread,
    and a dead peer does not delay the others.

