keel (0.23.57) unstable; urgency=medium

  * keel vip promote failed with "etcd did not take the claim: etcdctl
    txn: no answer within 10.5 s" on a poor link, and a second promote
    then failed with "keel-vip.service did not add the address to wg0
    within 15 s" (keel#135). The claim's transaction had one try, and a
    transaction that times out may have committed: then the claim was
    in etcd with a lease that no node renewed, so no controller carried
    the address. That second failure is a consequence of the first.
    Now, after a transaction that etcd did not answer in time, the
    counter is read first: this node's own claim at the epoch is the
    claim made; another claim ends the claim; an unchanged counter is
    tried again with the same comparison, never a blind write, at most
    3 times, none started 30 s after the first, a lease older than 10 s
    replaced first. The leases of the tries that did not win are
    revoked, so a late transaction with one of them fails. A promote
    that finds this node's own claim in etcd records it with its lease,
    so the controller renews the lease and carries the address.

