keel (0.23.27) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A returned old PostgreSQL primary no longer takes writes for 3 to
    4 s after a boot or a heal (keel#156). keel installs a drop-in for
    postgresql@.service that runs keel database guard as root before
    each start. On a VIP pair, the server starts as a primary only when
    this node's claim is proven, with the VIP on wg0. When the newest
    claim is the other member's, the guard writes standby.signal first,
    so the server starts as a standby that follows nobody. When this
    node's own claim is not proven (at boot), the start is refused, and
    keel database follow starts the server once the VIP is proven. On a
    node with no pair the guard does nothing.

