keel (0.23.22) unstable; urgency=medium

  * With etcd, an automatic failover of a PostgreSQL pair now gives a
    writable primary with no operator (keel#165). The maintainer decided
    it on 2026-10-15 (handbook 0054, amendment of 2026-10-15). When the
    VIP controller claims because the lease of the old primary's claim
    expired at its due time, it states that the old primary is gone,
    the same as keel database promote --old-primary-gone. The new
    primary then commits alone until a standby streams again. A revoked
    lease, or a lease that the controller never saw alive, states
    nothing, and the commits wait as before.
  * The statement carries the epoch of its claim. keel database follow
    removes a statement of another epoch unused.

