keel (0.23.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A cloud simple pair could not get its database certificate when the
    mesh's root CA was held by a third node (keel#105). Only etcd
    members wrote /var/lib/keel/etcd/holder, so each pair member asked
    the other one, which refused. Now every roster carries the root
    certificate its member holds and a notice of the holder's address,
    signed by the root's key (decision 0051). A member takes a notice
    only when it verifies with the root certificate it holds, so no
    member can send certificate requests to another address. A member
    with no root certificate takes one only from a roster that it
    fetched from a trust root, never from an announcement. A node that
    knows no holder fetches its peers' rosters before it asks. A notice
    dated more than 5 minutes ahead of the local clock is refused, and
    the notice has a region field (absent: the first region).

