keel (0.23.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A crashed old primary took writes after its boot (keel#104): keel
    database follow set read_only OFF from the claim of the VIP in the
    node's state file, before keel vip check learned that the other
    node held the VIP at a newer epoch. On a real pair the old primary
    was writable for 31 s. Now follow lifts read_only only when the VIP
    is on wg0, which keel adds only after a proof (a fresh claim, a
    peer's answer with no newer claim, or with etcd a lease renewal
    that the majority confirmed). Without the proof the server stays
    read only and locked, also when etcd or the peers do not answer at
    boot. Follow waits up to 15 s for the VIP, and the VIP's state is
    written again when keel adds the VIP, so follow runs again then.
  * A paired node with no claim of the VIP (its state file removed, or
    before the first promote) is not proven either: a declared primary
    stays read only and locked until a claim is proven. keel database
    watch follows a server again when it takes writes with no claim, or
    while the VIP is not on wg0 (its valid_lft ran out). One keel
    database follow runs at a time, under a lock.

