keel (0.12.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New module keel.manifest and commands keel manifest validate and keel
    manifest show: the reader of the appliance manifest, version 1
    (decision 0041, step 1 of its first implementation). One schema for
    overlay manifests, /usr/share/keel/overlays/<name>.yaml, and
    appliance manifests, /usr/share/keel/appliances/<name>.yaml, read
    under --root; unknown keys are refused at every level and every
    error is reported at once, with the exit codes of spec validate.
  * validate checks rules 1 to 24 of the format, and resolves each
    appliance along its base chain down to core: overlays once, every
    (port, protocol) once whatever the states, requires enabled in every
    mode, names once across the chain. A state written on, off, yes or
    no reaches PyYAML as a boolean and is refused with that reason; a
    key given twice in one mapping is refused rather than overwritten.
    A unit name has the shape systemd.unit(5) gives it, so none climbs
    out of the unit directories with "..", and an init script counts
    only as a regular executable file inside the root. Names and values
    are matched whole, so a trailing newline is refused. YAML nested past
    the recursion limit cannot be read (exit 2).
  * show prints a manifest, and with --resolved the overlays with their
    state per installation mode, the ports with their loopback, mesh or
    public exposure, the processes, checks, secrets and hooks of the
    chain. On Keel Web its first two tables are the format's.
  * Nothing else in keel reads a manifest yet.

